          ],
          "returnType": "Sound",
          "description": "The Sound for a named sprite - the playback side of Sound.addSprite. Same concept as Sound.clip, addressed by name instead of by offset: a sub-Sound over the same decoded buffer, with the clip's own loop flag and its own voice pool. The result is memoized per name, so the pool is shared across every play of that sprite and repeated lookups are free. It stays valid until the name is redefined, removed, or this sound is destroyed."
        }
